# S459 — hand-written prose for the 1 Enoch cards whose old note was degraded or whose claim no longer fits the live verse.
# The generator puts the full live verse (stand-alone italics, cited) in front of each of these. The verse carries; the prose points.
# Voice: direct, scripture-anchored, no internal references. Restored names with parentheticals. Son of Adam. English book names.

PROSE = {
# ---- Matthew ----
4274: "The Animal Apocalypse ends where the Magi's watch ends: a white bull born at the close of the vision, large-horned, feared and petitioned by every beast and bird — the seed of Adam restored in one figure. *Where is he that is born King of the Yahudim (Jews)? for we have seen his star in the east* (Matthew 2:2). The men who read the heavens were looking for the one this vision had already shown.",
4275: "The lamb that becomes the great horned one — the Lamb who is also the King. The star of Matthew 2:2 announced a child; the vision had already shown what the child would be: the lamb grown into the one the Lord of the sheep rejoices over.",
4292: "This is the room the open heaven of Matthew 3:16 gives onto — the lofty throne, the cherubim, the fire streaming from beneath it (1 Enoch 14:18–22). The heavens do not open onto emptiness; they open onto the throne of the Great Glory, and from that throne the voice of the next verse speaks.",
4293: "The ascent that ends in the Head of Days naming the Son of Adam (1 Enoch 71:14) begins here, with the heavens opened to Enoch. At the Yarden (Jordan) the same heavens open and the same Father speaks over the same Son.",
4299: "*And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased* (Matthew 3:17). Enoch had already heard the Father name him: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The voice at the river is the voice from the throne; the Son it names is the one righteousness never leaves.",
4323: "*Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 5:3). The blessing is not an entry fee; it is the Father's own word over those who are already his. Enoch heard the same word before the Beatitudes were spoken: peace, protection, mercy, belonging — pronounced over the elect, not offered to applicants.",
4328: "*Ye are the light of the world* (Matthew 5:14) — not *become*; *are.* Enoch says why: the righteous are set in the light of the sun and the elect in the light of eternal life. The light the disciples carry is the light they were placed in.",
4330: "*Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 5:16). Enoch saw the day the light appears on the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth — and the question that day asks of the sinners. The shining is the Father's doing; the glory goes to him.",
4334: "Enoch's charge to his children is the charge Matthew 5:19 makes to every teacher: do not alter the words of uprightness. *Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so, he shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven.* To alter the words and to teach men so are one act; both are named here before the gospel names them.",
4335: "Enoch knew the mystery before the pulpit practised it: sinners will alter and pervert the words of righteousness, and write books about it. *Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so* (Matthew 5:19) — the teaching is the perverting; the books are the sermons. The kingdom-status of such teachers was fixed long before the sermon was preached.",
4365: "Enoch's angels pray what the disciples are taught to pray: the holy and blessed name, the throne of glory that stands to all generations, the King of kings. *Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come* (Matthew 6:9–10) is the same prayer in the mouth of the children.",
4367: "The One whose kingdom the disciples pray to come is the One who made all things and holds power over all things, from whom nothing hides. *Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven* (Matthew 6:10) asks nothing new; it asks that what is already true in heaven be seen on earth.",
4377: "Two ways, and only two. Enoch sets them before his sons — the paths of righteousness worthy of acceptance, the paths of unrighteousness that vanish — long before Matthew 7:13's *wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction.* The choice at Deuteronomy 30:19 was already old when Enoch taught it.",
4378: "Enoch sees it from the other side: the paths of violence and death are shown to certain men of a generation, and they keep far from them. *Strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it* (Matthew 7:14). The few who hold themselves afar are the few who find.",
4391: "Enoch asks who *that Son of Adam* is — a figure named by title, standing beside the Head of Days. When Yahusha (Jesus) says *the Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20) he takes that title for himself: the named one of the Parables, now with no bed on the earth he came to.",
4395: "The spirits that met him among the tombs are named here by origin and by work: the spirits of the giants, afflicting and destroying, hungering and thirsting without food. The two possessed men of Matthew 8:28, *exceeding fierce, so that no man might pass by that way,* were under exactly this.",
4411: "*The Son of Adam hath power on earth to forgive sins* (Matthew 9:6). The Parables had already named him the one born unto righteousness, over whom righteousness abides; the forgiveness he speaks on earth is that abiding righteousness exercised in flesh.",
4424: "The shepherds who were set over the sheep and destroyed more than they were bidden end here, judged and cast into the fiery abyss. When Yahusha (Jesus) saw the multitudes *as sheep having no shepherd* (Matthew 9:36), he was looking at the flock those shepherds had left; the vision had already recorded their sentence.",
4425: "The shepherdless sheep of Matthew 9:36 are not left shepherdless. Enoch saw the Lord of the sheep bring a new house, greater and loftier than the first, with all the sheep within it. The compassion that moved him at the sight of the scattered flock is the compassion that builds the house.",
4426: "*When he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad* (Matthew 9:36). Enoch saw where the scattering ends: all that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in the house, and the Lord of the sheep rejoicing because they had returned.",
4453: "*Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 10:32). Enoch swears to the righteous that their names are already written before the glory of the Great One. The Son confesses before the Father the ones whose names were written before they ever confessed.",
4454: "*But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 10:33). Enoch's word to the righteous who die in righteousness is that their memorial does not perish before the Great One. The warning of Matthew 10:33 is the other side of that promise: a memorial can be kept, and a name can be blotted out (1 Enoch 108:3). The denier is not a tare who never had a name; he is wheat that did not endure.",
4461: "The answer sent to Yochanan (John) — *the blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, and the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them* (Matthew 11:5) — is the peace, protection, mercy, and light Enoch saw promised to the righteous, now arriving in flesh.",
4462: "Enoch saw the days when the righteous escape and complete their years in peace, the earth tilled in righteousness and cleansed of oppression (1 Enoch 10:17–22). The works Yahusha (Jesus) lists for Yochanan (John) at Matthew 11:5 are the first fruits of those days — the age Enoch saw, beginning.",
4501: "*Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him* (Matthew 12:14). Enoch's woe already names them: sinners who persecute the righteous, and the heavy yoke that waits for them. The council against the Righteous One is the act the woe was written for.",
4504: "*Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles* (Matthew 12:18). Enoch saw the same: the spirit of righteousness poured out on the Elect One seated on the throne, and the word of his mouth bringing judgment. The servant of Isaiah and the Elect One of the Parables are one figure, and the Spirit upon him is the same Spirit.",
4512: "*But the blasphemy against the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Ghost) shall not be forgiven unto men* (Matthew 12:32). Enoch heard the sentence on those who showed what was hidden and became the damned: no place of repentance for ever. There is a sin that closes the door from the inside; the Pharisees who called the Spirit's work the work of Beelzebub stood at that door.",
4526: "*Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given* (Matthew 13:11). Enoch says who the *you* are: the holy and righteous to whom the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits reveals him, who have hated this world of unrighteousness. The revealing follows the belonging; it does not create it.",
4531: "*Then cometh the wicked one, and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart* (Matthew 13:19). Enoch names the spirits of the Watchers assuming many forms, leading mankind astray — the actor behind the catching-away. He is not a figure of speech; the restored library records his origin and his end.",
4536: "*The tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). Enoch names them before the parable does: the children of the Watchers, a seed with a father of its own, distinguished from the line of Adam and marked for destruction. The tares are not bad wheat; they are another seed.",
4540: "*And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth* (Matthew 13:42). Enoch saw the abyss of fire and the prison appointed for the Watchers — the furnace the parable names, already mapped.",
4541: "*The reapers are the angels* (Matthew 13:39), and here they are by name: Michael, Gabriel, Raphael and Phanuel, casting the hosts of Azazel into the burning furnace on the great day. The furnace of Matthew 13:42 has its angels, its day, and its reason — vengeance for leading astray those who dwell on the earth.",
4545: "*All these things spake Yahusha (Jesus) unto the multitude in parables* (Matthew 13:34). Enoch had named the Son of Adam as the one who reveals all the treasures of that which is hidden. The parables are that revealing — hidden things opened, by the one chosen to open them.",
4557: "*The good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). The seed war is older than the parable. Enoch is shown the spirit of Hevel (Abel), the first righteous blood, making its suit against the seed of Qayin (Cain) until that seed is gone from among the seed of men. Two seeds, from Genesis 4 to the harvest.",
4597: "*Whom do men say that I the Son of Adam am?* (Matthew 16:13). The question uses the title Enoch asked about — *that Son of Adam,* the one who went with the Head of Days. The King asks whether men have recognized the figure the Parables named.",
4598: "*Thou art the Messiah (Christ), the Son of the living Elohim (God)* (Matthew 16:16). Kefa (Peter) confesses what Enoch was told: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has chosen, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. The confession at Caesarea Philippi is the angel's answer at 1 Enoch 46:3, spoken on earth.",
4602: "*I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 16:19). The secrets of righteousness belong to the Elect One who stands before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits; the keys Kefa (Peter) receives are stewardship of what is his. The one who holds the secrets delegates their opening.",
4603: "*I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 16:19). Enoch saw the Elect One seated on the Father's throne, his mouth pouring out the secrets of wisdom and counsel. The keys are given by the one who sits on that throne; the house of David's key (Isaiah 22:22) is on his shoulder before it is in Kefa's (Peter's) hand.",
4604: "*Flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 16:17). The Father's naming of the Son of Adam at 1 Enoch 71:14 is the same revealing — the Head of Days declaring who he is. Kefa (Peter) receives on earth what Enoch heard in heaven, and the keys follow the revealing.",
4605: "*Whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven* (Matthew 16:19). The sum of judgement was given to the Son of Adam on the throne of his glory; what the apostles bind and loose is bound and loosed under that judgement, not beside it.",
4677: "*Whoso shall offend one of these little ones which believe in me, it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck* (Matthew 18:6). The stumbling-blocks laid across the way of the little ones have a history: Azazel taught men the arts that became the snares. The millstone is the King's answer to the teacher of the snare.",
4680: "*It were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and that he were drowned in the depth of the sea* (Matthew 18:6). Better than what? Than the place Enoch was shown — spirits set apart in great pain until the great day of judgement, and bound there. The sea is the lesser end.",
4682: "*For the Son of Adam is come to save that which was lost* (Matthew 18:11). The Lord of the sheep comes to the flock in person, staff in hand, and the beasts and birds that devoured them are swallowed by the earth. The saving of the lost is the Lord of the sheep arriving.",
4683: "*If a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?* (Matthew 18:12). Enoch's vision names the owner of the flock: Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, whose house and tower the sheep forsook. The shepherd of the parable is not a hired man; he is the Lord of the sheep seeking his own.",
4685: "*He rejoiceth more of that sheep, than of the ninety and nine which went not astray* (Matthew 18:13). Enoch saw that joy at the end: the Lord of the sheep rejoicing with great joy because all that had been dispersed had returned to his house. The parable's one sheep is the vision's whole flock.",
4686: "*In heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 18:10). Enoch is given the names of the four who stand before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits — mercy, healing, power, and repentance unto hope. The little ones are watched over from the throne itself.",
4711: "*A rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 19:23). Enoch's woe says why: those who trust in riches depart from them, having not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of their wealth. The difficulty is not the money; it is the trust.",
4712: "*A rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 19:23). The young ruler's confidence — *all these things have I kept from my youth up* — is the sinner's confidence Enoch names: a remembrance that is evil against him, however secure the holdings look.",
4713: "*It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of Elohim (God)* (Matthew 19:24). Enoch gives the rich man's own speech — silver gathered, granaries full, *let us do what we purposed.* That speech is the needle's eye closing.",
4715: "*With men this is impossible; but with Elohim (God) all things are possible* (Matthew 19:26). Enoch saw the day the children of the earth understand that riches cannot save them. What riches cannot do, Elohim (God) does — that is the whole of the disciples' hope, and the whole of the rich man's.",
4726: "*So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen* (Matthew 20:16). Enoch saw the chosen gathered: the congregation of the elect and holy sown, and all the elect standing before him on that day. The few are not fewer because they tried harder; they are the elect, and the elect are revealed by their standing.",
4736: "*The Son of Adam came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The same Son of Adam, Enoch saw, raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. The one who serves is the one who judges; the ransom and the reckoning belong to the same hands.",
4753: "*Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever. And presently the fig tree withered away* (Matthew 21:19). Enoch saw the Lord of the sheep do the same to a flock that had abandoned him: unmoved, leaving them to be devoured. The withered tree is the leadership that bore no fruit, left to its own harvest.",
4761: "*He will miserably destroy those wicked men, and will let out his vineyard unto other husbandmen* (Matthew 21:41). The husbandmen answer their own parable; Enoch's vision records the sentence they pronounced — the seventy shepherds judged, found guilty, and cast into the fiery abyss.",
4782: "*Yahuah (The LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand* (Matthew 22:44; Psalm 110:1). Enoch heard the same seating spoken by the Father: *the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne.* The Pharisees could not say how David's son is David's Lord; the Parables had already seated him.",
4783: "*Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool* (Matthew 22:44). The Head of Days placing the Elect One on the throne of glory is Psalm 110:1 seen from the throne room — the Father seating the Son, the Son judging. The Formless seats the Formed; the One who is seated is Elohim (God) and has a Father.",
4784: "*If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?* (Matthew 22:45). The Father answers at 1 Enoch 71:14: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* Born — David's son after the flesh; named by the Head of Days — David's Lord. The question the Pharisees could not answer, the Parables had answered.",
4801: "*Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of Gehinnom (hell)?* (Matthew 23:33). Enoch was shown the prison of the angels and told it holds them for ever. The judgment the serpents cannot escape is the judgment their fathers, the Watchers, are already held for; the seed goes where the seed came from.",
4802: "*That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Hevel (Abel)* (Matthew 23:35). Enoch saw the spirit of Hevel (Abel) making its suit against the seed of Qayin (Cain) until that seed is destroyed. The blood that cries from the ground (Genesis 4:10) is still crying in Enoch's vision, and the King hands the sum of it to the generation standing in front of him.",
4807: "*As in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noach (Noah) entered into the ark* (Matthew 24:38). Enoch heard the sentence pronounced over those days: judgement determined, not to be withheld, the earth and its dwellers to be destroyed for the sorceries they had learned. The eating and drinking went on under a sentence already passed.",
4808: "*And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:39). The flood took the wicked away; it did not carry the righteous off. Enoch's word for the Watchers is the same taking: led off to the abyss of fire, to the prison. The ones taken at the coming are the ones taken at the flood — the judged.",
4814: "*And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds* (Matthew 24:31). Enoch saw the gathering as a flock: the great horn cried to the sheep, their eyes opened, and the rams all ran to it. The gathering is the sheep running to the horn that called them.",
4845: "*When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory* (Matthew 25:31). Enoch saw that seat and the faces of those who see it — terror, pain, downcast countenance, when they see that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory. The sheep-and-goats judgment opens on the throne the Parables had already set.",
4846: "*And all the holy angels with him* (Matthew 25:31). Enoch gives the roll: the host of the heavens, the holy ones above, Cherubim, Seraphim and Ophannim, the angels of power and of principalities — and the Elect One among them. The company of the coming was mustered in the Parables before the gospel named it.",
4847: "*And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another* (Matthew 25:32). The Son of Adam who separates is the Son of Adam Enoch saw raise the kings and the mighty from their seats and break the teeth of the sinners. The separation is a reversal; the mighty do not keep their seats at it.",
4848: "*Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels* (Matthew 25:41). Enoch saw what that departure is for the strong: countenance put down, shame, darkness for a dwelling, worms for a bed, no hope of rising — because they did not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.",
4849: "*Depart from me, ye cursed* (Matthew 25:41) is answered in Enoch by the mouths of the kings and the mighty themselves: in the day of their tribulation he saves them not, and their confession comes too late to be anything but true. *Lord, when saw we thee an hungred?* (Matthew 25:44) is the same late confession.",
4850: "*Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Matthew 26:64). The bound man before the council names himself with Enoch's title — *that Son of Adam* who went with the Head of Days. The council thought it was judging him; he was telling them who would judge.",
4854: "*Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* (Matthew 26:64). Enoch saw what the council will see: all the kings and the mighty falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, petitioning him for mercy. The men who condemned him will kneel to him.",
4877: "*When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against Yahusha (Jesus) to put him to death* (Matthew 27:1). Enoch saw the other morning: all the kings and the mighty standing up in that day to see and recognize how he sits on the throne of his glory, where no lying word is spoken. The council that condemned him stands at his bar.",
4878: "*If he be the King of Yashar'el (Israel), let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him* (Matthew 27:42). The mockers set the wrong test. Enoch saw the King's credential: the whole host of heaven summoned, and the Elect One among them. He did not come down from the cross; he is the one for whom the heavens are mustered.",
4879: "*He trusted in Elohim (God); let him deliver him now, if he will have him* (Matthew 27:43). The Head of Days had already said it: *the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.* The cross was not the Father's forsaking of the Son; it was the Son of Adam, born unto righteousness, doing what righteousness does.",
4880: "*Let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him* (Matthew 27:42). Enoch saw the mockers' end: the kings and the mighty and those who rule the earth falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, worshipping and petitioning. *Every knee should bow* (Philippians 2:10) — the mockers included.",
4900: "*All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch saw the giving: the Elect One seated on the throne of glory, the spirit of righteousness poured out on him, the word of his mouth slaying the sinners. The power was given by the Father; the Son wields it.",
4901: "*All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch's Son of Adam raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. That is what all power looks like when it is used.",
4902: "*All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch saw the placing — Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits setting the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge and to weigh deeds in the balance. The Father is the giver; the Son is seated; the power is the power to judge.",
# ---- Mark ----
7852: "*And see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid* (Mark 5:15). The man restored is the reversal, in one life, of what Enoch says these spirits do — defile mankind and lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods. Their day of judgement is fixed; the Gadarene was given his back early.",
7856: "*And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea* (Mark 5:13). The spirits of the giants afflict and destroy, Enoch says, and they do not eat yet hunger. The sea was not their judgement; that waits for the day of the consummation. It was the King displacing them.",
7857: "*My name is Legion: for we are many* (Mark 5:9). Enoch names what a legion does to a man among the tombs: the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, and cause offences. The man crying and cutting himself night and day was under exactly that.",
7858: "*My name is Legion: for we are many* (Mark 5:9). Many, because they are the earth-born spirits of the giants whose dwelling is on the earth. The gospel's word for them is *Legion*; Enoch's word is their pedigree.",
7869: "*Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched* (Mark 9:48). Enoch was shown where the sinners' spirits are set apart in great pain until the great day of judgement — a holding until the judgement comes, and then the binding for ever. The place Mark warns of is the place Enoch had mapped; the fire that is not quenched is the judgement the holding waits for.",
7874: "*Ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Mark 14:62). Enoch saw the seeing: the kings and the mighty falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, petitioning for mercy. The court that condemned him will see him, exactly as he said.",
7876: "*Sitting on the right hand of power* (Mark 14:62). Enoch saw the placing: Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits set the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. The bound man names his seat before the court that thinks it is judging him.",
7877: "*Ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Mark 14:62). The one the Sanhedrin condemns is the one Enoch saw raise the kings and the mighty from their seats and break the teeth of the sinners. The reversal was written before the trial.",
# ---- Luke ----
7924: "*I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven* (Luke 10:18). Enoch records the first fall — two hundred who descended on Hermon in the days of Jared and bound themselves by oath. The seventy returning with the devils subject to them (Luke 10:17) were undoing, territory by territory, what began on that mountain.",
7938: "*For the Son of Adam is come to seek and to save that which was lost* (Luke 19:10). Enoch saw the seeking as a horn crying to the sheep, their eyes opening, and all of them running to it. The lost are the house of Yashar'el (Israel) scattered among the nations; the seeking is the call that brings the sheep running home — not a new flock gathered from the nations.",
7946: "*Between us and you there is a great gulf fixed* (Luke 16:26). Enoch saw the fixing: the hollow places made to receive the dead until the day of their judgement, divided one from another. Sheol is real and the dead are aware in it — and it is a holding until the appointed period, not the final destination.",
7956: "*To day shalt thou be with me in paradise* (Luke 23:43). Enoch was shown the hollow places where the spirits of the dead are received — deep, wide, divided. The paradise promised to the thief that day is the righteous division of those places, where the bright spring of water is, until the day of judgement.",
7957: "*Neither can they die any more: for they are equal unto the angels* (Luke 20:36). Enoch tells the righteous to hope, *for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.* The equality with angels is joy without end, promised before the Sadducees asked their question.",
7958: "*Equal unto the angels; and are the children of Elohim (God), being the children of the resurrection* (Luke 20:36). Enoch saw their dwellings with the righteous angels and their resting-places with the holy. The children of the resurrection dwell where Enoch saw them dwell.",
# ---- John, Acts, epistles ----
7969: "*He came unto his own, and his own received him not* (John 1:11). Enoch saw Wisdom go out to make her dwelling among the children of men and find no place. The Word came to his own and found no room; the rejection was foreseen before the Word was made flesh.",
7997: "*And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw him lift up his countenance to judge their secret ways, and the whole host bless the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for it. The authority is given by the Father; the judging is the Son's; the praise returns to the Father.",
7998: "*And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw the giving: the Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge and to weigh deeds in the balance. The authority John names is the seat Enoch saw filled.",
8001: "*The hour is come, that the Son of Adam should be glorified* (John 12:23). Enoch saw the glorifying: the Son of Adam judging their secret ways, and all the holy blessing and sanctifying the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. *Father, glorify thy name* (John 12:28) is the Son asking for what the Parables already showed.",
8002: "*The hour is come, that the Son of Adam should be glorified* (John 12:23). The Son of Adam is the one the Head of Days named at 1 Enoch 71:14 — born unto righteousness, never forsaken. The hour John names is the hour that naming comes to pass on earth.",
8008: "*I am the resurrection, and the life* (John 11:25). Enoch saw the earth and Sheol give back what they hold, and the Elect One arise. The one who says *I am the resurrection* is the one at whose arising the dead are given back.",
9875: "The coming the angels promise at Acts 1:11 — *this same Yahusha (Jesus)... shall so come in like manner* — is the coming Jude quoted from Enoch: he comes with ten thousands of his holy ones to execute judgement. The holy ones with him are the seed of promise, gathered to him and coming with him into the land — not souls come down out of heaven.",
9899: "*Yahuah (The LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand* (Acts 2:34). Enoch saw the seating: Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placing the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. The right hand of Psalm 110 is the throne of glory of the Parables.",
9900: "*Elohim (God) hath made that same Yahusha (Jesus), whom ye have crucified, both Lord and Messiah (Christ)* (Acts 2:36). The Father had already named him: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The one Kefa (Peter) preaches is the one the Head of Days declared.",
12616: "*By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death... because Elohim (God) had translated him* (Hebrews 11:5). The Torah says only that Elohim (God) took him; Enoch tells the taking from the inside — *my spirit was translated and it ascended into the heavens.* The man who pleased Elohim (God) was brought up among the holy sons of Elohim (God), translated rather than buried.",
52065: "*Whose names are in the book of life* (Philippians 4:3). Enoch swears to the righteous that their names are written before the glory of the Great One. Paul's fellow-labourers are written there; the writing was done in heaven, and the labour on earth reveals it.",
56509: "*Which delivered us from the wrath to come* (1 Thessalonians 1:10). Enoch names who the wrath is for: the hard-hearted who have not done the commandments of Yahuah (Lord) and shall find no peace. The Thessalonians are delivered from that, not because wrath is cancelled, but because they are not the hard-hearted; the next verse (1 Enoch 1:8) gives the righteous their peace.",
56538: "*At the coming of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13). Enoch carried the word long before Thessalonica: he comes with ten thousands of his holy ones to execute judgement upon all. It is the very prophecy Jude quotes by name as Enoch's; the day he comes with his holy ones is the day the ungodly are convicted.",
56571: "*Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness* (1 Thessalonians 5:5). Enoch saw the division made final: the darkness first destroyed, and a light that never ends established before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The children of the day inherit that light; the night they are not of is the darkness that is destroyed.",
# ---- Revelation ----
12820: "The throne Enoch saw — crystal, wheels like the sun, cherubim, fire streaming from beneath it (1 Enoch 14:18–22) — is the throne-and-fire presence John is brought into when he sees the Formed One whose *eyes were as a flame of fire* and whose *feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace* (Revelation 1:14–15). John falls as dead, as Enoch fell on his face.",
12826: "The restored library says plainly what the letter promises: the fruit of the tree *shall be for food to the elect,* and the tree transplanted to the holy place. *To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God)* (Revelation 2:7). The same elect, the same tree, the same gift.",
12850: "*I will not blot out his name out of the book of life* (Revelation 3:5). Enoch swears that the names of the righteous are written before the glory of the Great One — and warns that names can be blotted out: *their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books* (1 Enoch 108:3). No name is added later; names written before the foundation of the world are kept by overcoming, or lost.",
12942: "*And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone* (Revelation 4:3). Enoch saw the lofty throne of crystal with wheels like the shining sun and the cherubim about it, and the Great Glory seated on it (1 Enoch 14:20). The throne of precious stone was seen before the door in heaven opened to John.",
12953: "The praise Enoch heard rises *for ever and ever* — the very note John's four living creatures sound, who *rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8). One worship before one throne.",
13370: "Enoch is shown the end of heaven and earth, a prison for the stars and the host of heaven. John sees *a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). The pit has a history; the stars it holds are named in the next verses (1 Enoch 18:15–16).",
13372: "*There arose a smoke out of the pit, as the smoke of a great furnace* (Revelation 9:2). Enoch had seen the abyss cleft and blazing with columns of fire — the furnace-place. The smoke of Revelation's pit rises from the fire Enoch was shown.",
13414: "*The mystery of Elohim (God) should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets* (Revelation 10:7). Enoch is set before the heavenly tablets and told to read what is written there and mark every fact. The mystery is what stands written in heaven; the prophets read it and declare it, and the seventh trumpet brings it to pass.",
13415: "*The mystery of Elohim (God) should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets* (Revelation 10:7). Enoch read the heavenly tablets and the book of all the deeds of mankind to the remotest generations. The prophet does not invent the mystery; he reads it where it is already written.",
13799: "*Whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world* (Revelation 13:8). Enoch saw the books opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne, and elsewhere *the books of the living were opened before Him* (1 Enoch 47:3). The worshippers of the beast are not in that book; the names in it were written before the beast rose.",
13805: "*As many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed* (Revelation 13:15). Enoch saw the end of every beast and bird that devoured the sheep: the Lord of the sheep came with the staff of his wrath and the earth swallowed them. The beast and the false prophet go into the fire (Revelation 19:20); the beasts of the vision go into the earth. The fire the false prophet calls down is not the fire that has the last word.",
14898: "*The books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life* (Revelation 20:12). Enoch saw the sealed books taken and opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne, and in the Parables *the books of the living were opened before Him* (1 Enoch 47:3). The books of deeds and the book of the living, opened together for judgment, are the books of the great white throne.",
14941: "Enoch was shown the tree of life transplanted to the holy place, its fruit for food to the elect. John sees the transplanting done — the tree *in the midst of the street* of the city, *and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations* (Revelation 22:2). The fruit reserved for the elect is theirs; the leaves reach the nations through them.",
15003: "Enoch saw the four John sees: four presences on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, whose praises he heard (1 Enoch 40:3). John's *four beasts* who *rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8) are the same four about the same throne.",
15091: "*Whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb* (Revelation 13:8). Enoch knows the book and the blotting: *their names shall be blotted out of the book of life.* The names were written before the foundation of the world; the beast's worshippers are not among them, and the wheat that falls away is blotted out. No name is added after.",
15167: "*That he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled* (Revelation 20:3). Enoch saw the rebels bound *till the time when their guilt should be consummated* — a fixed term, after which comes the final fire. The binding of the dragon has the same shape: a term, then the end.",
# ---- Tanakh and other sources ----
56650: "*Ask of me, and I shall give thee the heathen for thine inheritance* (Psalm 2:8). The King who asks is the Elect One Enoch saw placed on the throne of glory by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The inheritance is given to the one who is seated.",
56652: "*Why do the heathen rage... The kings of the earth set themselves* (Psalm 2:1–2). Enoch saw where the raging ends: the mighty and the kings imploring for a little respite from the angels of punishment, that they might fall down and confess. He that sits in the heavens laughs (Psalm 2:4).",
57410: "*Yea, all kings shall fall down before him: all nations shall serve him* (Psalm 72:11). The King they fall before is the Elect One Enoch saw placed on the throne of glory to judge. The nations serve the one who is seated.",
66488: "*I saw Yahuah (the Lord) sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple* (Isaiah 6:1). Enoch saw the Great Glory seated, his raiment brighter than the sun and whiter than snow. The train that filled the temple is the raiment Enoch could not look upon.",
66489: "*I saw Yahuah (the Lord) sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up* (Isaiah 6:1). Enoch saw the same lofty throne — crystal, wheels like the shining sun, cherubim — and the Glory none could approach (1 Enoch 14:20–21). The prophet and the patriarch stood before one throne.",
66492: "*The whole earth is full of his glory* (Isaiah 6:3) is sung in heaven without ceasing: the first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever. One worship, in heaven and over all the earth.",
69749: "*For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth* (Isaiah 65:17). Enoch heard the same promise from the same mouth: the heaven transformed into an eternal blessing and light, the earth transformed into a blessing, the Elect One dwelling among his people. The prophet's new creation is the age of the Parables.",
69783: "*By fire and by his sword will Yahuah (the LORD) plead with all flesh* (Isaiah 66:16); *neither shall their fire be quenched* (Isaiah 66:24). Enoch sees the sinners given into the hands of the elect, burning as straw before the face of the holy, sinking as lead before the face of the righteous. The fire that closes Isaiah is the fire of the Parables.",
69795: "*As the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me* (Isaiah 66:22). Enoch heard Yahuah (Lord) promise to transform the heaven and the earth and set his elect upon it, the sinners shut out. The renewal in which the seed and the name remain is the renewal the Parables saw.",
77220: "*The chariots of Elohim (God) are twenty thousand, even thousands of angels: Yahuah (the Lord) is among them, as in Sinai* (Psalm 68:17): the psalm's thousands are angels, the chariotry of the coming One. Enoch's ten thousands of holy ones are another company — the seed of promise, gathered and coming with him into the land (Zechariah 14:5). The angels attend him; his saints come with him.",
165963: "*He came with ten thousands of saints* (Deuteronomy 33:2). Enoch's ten thousands of holy ones are the same accompanying host — the verse Jude later quotes by name. The Formed One comes attended by the holy ones.",
# ---- Enoch-as-source and extracanon cards (labelled style: the generator writes '1 Enoch c:v — *verse*' first) ----
4258: "The Father seats the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. *They shall call his name Immanuel, which being interpreted is, Elohim (God) with us* (Matthew 1:23) — the enthroned one is the one who came in flesh.",
4259: "*Thou shalt call his name Yahusha (Jesus): for he shall save his people from their sins* (Matthew 1:21). The name revealed to the holy ones in heaven, to their joy, is the name given on earth to the child. The name is the gospel.",
7844: "*Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Yahusha (Jesus) of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us?* (Mark 1:24). The spirits that cry out have been told their sentence: no peace. The Holy One's coming is the disturbance of a peace they were never granted.",
12822: "*I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore* (Revelation 1:18). The one who says it is the Son of Adam born unto righteousness, over whom righteousness abides, whom the Head of Days never forsakes — forsaken not even in death.",
15036: "*I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). Enoch was told who is bound in that place: stars of heaven that transgressed the commandment, bound till their ten thousand years are consummated. The pit has prisoners before it has a key.",
15035: "*There arose a smoke out of the pit, as the smoke of a great furnace* (Revelation 9:2). Enoch saw the abyss with its columns of heavenly fire beyond measure. The smoke rises from a fire that was seen before the pit was opened.",
135969: "*And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw the sum of judgement given to the Son of Adam on the throne of his glory. The authority is given — by the Father — and it is given to the Son of Adam by that name.",
135440: "*Hereafter shall the Son of Adam sit on the right hand of the power of Elohim (God)* (Luke 22:69). Enoch saw the faces of those who see that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory — terror and pain. The council heard the claim; the vision shows them seeing it kept.",
22503: "Those who walk in the 364-day order of 74:13 are the righteous of 82:4; those who sin in the reckoning are the men of 82:5, at fault, not reckoning the four days. The order has two sides, and Enoch names both.",
25692: "Jubilees 6:37 names the disturbing of the order outright — feasts confounded, the unclean day made holy. Enoch names its root: men at fault who do not reckon the four intercalary days, and so lose the year.",
22500: "To complete the years *with righteousness* (74:13) is to walk as the righteous of this blessing walk — not sinning as the sinners in the reckoning of their days.",
22579: "The blessing on those who keep the commandments (81:10) is given its calendar here: blessed are those who do not sin in the reckoning of their days. Keeping the commandments includes keeping the count.",
22580: "The charge to preserve and not alter (81:10) rests on this: the reckoning Uriel showed is accurate and exact, and the host of heaven is subject to Yahuah (Lord). What is exact is not to be amended.",
25549: "Enoch's woe over the sinners who die in their sins is the woe the closing chapter (108) carries to its end.",
25412: "What 98:7 warns — that every sin is seen in heaven — 104:7 confirms against the sinners' own denial: all of it is written down, every day.",
16298: "The heading of the very document Enoch writes out and reads before Elohim (God) in 13:6 and 13:10 — a book of reprimand, not of pardon.",
48751: "As Enoch alone saw the vision of the ends of all things, so Abraham is fed only by the angel's speech, sustained by the sight he is about to be given.",
29120: "The whirlwind that carried Enoch off from the earth is the whirlwind Jasher 3:36 gives for his ascent, told here by Enoch himself.",
48743: "As Enoch was lifted by the winds and borne into heaven, so the angel bears Abraham up on the wings of the bird to be shown heaven and earth.",
48786: "Abraham too is borne up as with many winds to the borders of the flaming fire (Apocalypse of Abraham 15:4); the wind-borne ascent is the shared pattern of the prophets caught up to heaven.",
48824: "Enoch too was lifted up by the winds and borne into heaven to behold the throne, the throne of fire Abraham sees in his own ascent.",
55283: "The year left to Enoch to teach his children and record it for them is the charge behind the books of Enoch's handwriting a later generation reads in 2 Enoch 35:2.",
46048: "The living tree behind the sword in 1 Adam and Eve 54:4 is this fragrant tree Enoch was shown — the tree no mortal may touch until the great judgement, when it is given to the righteous (1 Enoch 25:4–5).",
4298: "*And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son* (Matthew 3:17). Enoch heard two voices in the throne room: the first blessing Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits (1 Enoch 40:4), the second blessing the Elect One. The Father's voice at the river and the heaven's blessing of the Elect One speak of the same Son.",
4329: "*A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid* (Matthew 5:14). Enoch saw the day the light appears on the face of the holy, righteous and elect, and the powerful can no longer behold it. The disciples on the mountain are the first sight of that city; the light that makes it visible is the Lord of Spirits' own.",
4366: "*Hallowed be thy name* (Matthew 6:9). Enoch's own prayer blesses the King whose dominion is through all generations and whose throne is the heavens. The disciples are taught to pray what the patriarch prayed.",
4386: "*Many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Avraham (Abraham), and Yitschaq (Isaac), and Ya'aqov (Jacob), in the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 8:11). Enoch saw the sitting-down: all that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in the house, and the Lord of the sheep rejoicing because they had returned. The many from east and west are the dispersed of the house coming home — the scattered sheep, not a new flock.",
17245: "Enoch's own Luminaries section widens chapter 34's three-per-quarter gates into the twelve portals of the winds.",
22549: "The thirty days the moon falls behind the sun and stars in five years is the lunar shortfall 78:4–5 records; the solar order leads, the moon lags.",
22559: "The same lag of the moon behind the sun Enoch already gave in the courses of the luminaries — the solar year is the primary order.",
55177: "The moon falling thirty days behind the sun in five years is the very deficiency Enoch's own Astronomical Book reckoned.",
55179: "The moon's reckoning through its gates, written down to the fifteenth day, is the lunar course Enoch's own Astronomical Book had already set down through the portals.",
25691: "The same 364-day order, completed *with perfect justice,* that Jubilees 6:32 says must not disturb its feasts.",

145067: "*They are exalted for a little while, but are gone and brought low* (Job 24:24). Enoch's woe to the mighty who oppress the righteous says the same: the day of their destruction is coming. The might does not keep.",
15005: "*Him that liveth for ever and ever* (Revelation 4:9) sits in a house Enoch saw: a structure built of crystals with tongues of living fire between them (1 Enoch 71:5), encircled by angels beyond counting. It is the throne-room John enters.",
120469: "*They that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament... as the stars for ever and ever* (Daniel 12:3). Enoch tells the righteous the same: they shall shine as the lights of heaven, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to them.",
7955: "*To day shalt thou be with me in paradise* (Luke 23:43). Enoch was shown the places made to receive the dead until the day of their judgement. The paradise promised to the thief that day is the righteous division of those places, held until the great judgement — not the final state, but the keeping until it.",
7892: "*Suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising Elohim (God)* (Luke 2:13). Enoch saw that host where it stands — thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. At the birth of the Son the host that stands before the throne came down to the fields.",
12956: "*The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne* (Revelation 4:10). Enoch saw the multitude beyond number standing before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The elders who cast their crowns belong to that numberless worship.",
12979: "*Ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands* (Revelation 5:11) — John's count is Enoch's count, word for word. Enoch heard that host bless Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits and bless the Elect One beside him (1 Enoch 40:4–5); John hears them cry *Worthy is the Lamb that was slain* (Revelation 5:12). The Father and the Lamb, praised together by the myriads.",
15015: "*Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing* (Revelation 5:12). The dignity the Lamb receives is the seat Enoch saw given: the Elect One placed on the throne of glory by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, to judge. The Lamb receives; the Father gives.",
49285: "Enoch's ascent to the lofty throne and the Glory none of flesh could behold is the elder pattern of Isaiah's angel from the seventh heaven (6:13) — it ain't new.",
49384: "Enoch too was brought before the lofty throne whose Glory none of flesh could behold — it ain't new.",
157298: "*I saw Yahuah (the LORD) sitting on his throne, and all the host of heaven standing by him* (1 Kings 22:19). Enoch saw the same throne — lofty, crystal, cherubim about it, ten thousand times ten thousand before him (1 Enoch 14:22). The restored witness joins the prophets: Yahuah (Lord) is enthroned in the heights, the host attending.",
60447: "*Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness* (2 Peter 2:4). Enoch was shown the place and told what it is. The apostle points to the prison the library shows.",
18922: "The Father places the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge and weigh deeds — the same throne-of-glory judgement 45:3 announces.",
18995: "The Son of Adam named in 48:2 is the Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge.",
19007: "The office of judging the secret things named in 49:4 is the throne-of-glory judgement given here.",
19972: "The next chapter repeats the enthronement and adds what is poured out on him: the spirit of righteousness, and the word of his mouth that slays the sinners.",
90046: "*Yahuah (The LORD) reigneth, he is clothed with majesty... the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved* (Psalm 93:1). The restored witness shows the reign as the Father placing the Son on the throne of glory to judge; the One who reigns is the One who seats, and the One seated is the Formed.",
135426: "*That ye may eat and drink at my table in my kingdom, and sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel)* (Luke 22:30). The Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge is the Son of Adam who shares that seat with the twelve.",
13836: "*One sat like unto the Son of Adam* (Revelation 14:14) — the comparative preserved: one *like* the Son of Adam, and the Standard he is like is the one Enoch heard named: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The crowned cloud-rider is that Son of Adam, who took flesh and remains the Formed.",
55168: "The sun's gates that 2 Enoch 14:2 counts are the portals Enoch's own Astronomical Book numbers — the great portal, the fourth, where the sun rises in the first month.",
7906: "*What have I to do with thee, Yahusha (Jesus), thou Son of Elohim (God) most high? I beseech thee, torment me not* (Luke 8:28). The spirits know the day of the consummation is appointed for them; Enoch records that they destroy only until it. The demoniac's cry is the fear of a sentence already written.",
16669: "Enoch revisits the prison of the stars later in the journey: the same binding until the ten thousand years are consummated that 18:16 first recorded.",
22534: "The second journey repeats the first: the stars that transgressed the commandment, bound — the prison of the transgressing stars seen at 18:15, seen again.",
21407: "The ascent of the spirit in chapter 71 follows the raising aloft of Enoch's name in 70:1 — two tellings of one taking-up, the climax of the Parables.",
}
PROSE = {k: v for k, v in PROSE.items() if v is not None}
